  "design": {
    "decision": "Low cards become the team's top cards in every suit, so the owner bids on [2]s through [6]s, keeps them as winners, and sheds honors instead.",
    "opponent": "Answerable: once it is revealed, opponents void a suit and trump the low winners, lead [♠] to pull low trumps early, or let the owner's partner overtake their own low card.",
    "rationale": "Keeps the legendary rule change and the Low Cards identity but drops the over-trump clause, so trumping and voiding are a real counter; it uses the standard [2]-through-[6] range, and the range itself is the power knob (it subsumes uc-twos-beat, so they should not stack in offers).",
